# Planned data layers

Use **one tile file per layer** (or per logical group) so regions can rebuild and toggle independently. Do **not** put harbours or seamarks into `marinas.json.gz`.

## Mooring & shelter

| Layer id | OSM / Overpass | Tile file | Concept | UI |
|----------|----------------|-----------|---------|-----|
| `osm-marinas` | `leisure=marina`, `seamark:type=marina` | `marinas.json.gz` | Actionable mooring | Tappable; “anchor here” context |
| `osm-harbours` | `seamark:type=harbour`, `harbour=yes` on `place=*` where useful | `harbours.json.gz` | Shelter / port of refuge, not a berth | Tappable; info only |
| `osm-anchorage` | `seamark:type=anchorage`, `seamark:anchorage:category=*` | `anchorages.json.gz` | Designated anchoring | Tappable |

## Place names (coastal geography)

Merge into **`highres.json.gz`** (with GeoNames) **or** a dedicated `osm-places.json.gz` if we need separate rebuild/toggle. Prefer **highres merge** for label de-duplication and one “place names” toggle; use a separate file only if build size or refresh cadence differs.

| Layer id | OSM / Overpass | Storage | UI |
|----------|----------------|---------|-----|
| `osm-bay` | `natural=bay` | highres (or `osm-places.json.gz`) | Tappable bay names |
| `osm-cape` | `natural=cape` | ↑ | Tappable headlands |
| `osm-island` | `place=island`, `place=islet` | ↑ | Tappable islands |
| `osm-strait` | `natural=strait` | ↑ | Optional — narrow water labels |

## Navigation aids (seamarks)

| Layer id | OSM / Overpass | Tile file | UI |
|----------|----------------|-----------|-----|
| `osm-seamarks-buoys` | `seamark:type=buoy`, `seamark:type=beacon`, lateral/cardinal/specialized buoy tags | `seamarks.json.gz` | Tappable; show `seamark:buoy:*`, colour, name |
| `osm-seamarks-lights` | `seamark:type=light_major`, `light_minor`, `seamark:light:*` | `lights.json.gz` or same file with `kind` property | Tappable; **future:** animate flash sequence from `seamark:light:sequence` |
| `osm-seamarks-other` | `seamark:type=notice`, `seamark:type=restricted_area`, fairway, pipeline, cable | `seamarks.json.gz` | Tappable warnings / info |

**Admin job:** `/admin/jobs/seamarks` (future) — same region/grid pattern as marinas; consider **smaller bboxes** or **higher grid step** first (buoys are dense in harbours).

**Light animation:** only meaningful for vector lights with OSM `seamark:light:sequence` / `seamark:light:period` tags; keep as a later map enhancement, not part of the build job.

## Optional / lower priority

| Layer id | Notes |
|----------|--------|
| `osm-wrecks` | `seamark:type=wreck`, `historic=wreck` — safety |
| `osm-fairway` | Line geometry; needs LineString tiles, not just points |
| `naturalearth` | Coastline/context (disabled in current geo build) |

